Which brings us to the subject of base camps.

It's worth setting up at least a main stash somewhere (preferrably in a
chest/box on a square with Elbereth permanently burned on it).  In a
coaligned temple (Minetown isn't great since it's often a long hike) is
perfect (safe haven for changing/enchanting armor, etc).  More likely,
the first level of Sokoban is convenient (you won't forget about it, if
you get the Eye you can gate back there instantaneously, etc) or
failing that a level with an altar (and a closet to lock yourself in
for changing armor, etc).

But earlier in the game, even just leaving it in a chest near a
downstairs is fine.  In addition to safeguarding all your unID'd
potions/scrolls until you at least have a sack to keep them safe it, it
also lets you jettison lots of weight and gives you a spot to keep all
those elven cloaks/boots/etc you find for later polymorphing.

